"The volume alarm with 12 hours of history: the baseline published in v2.2.0.",
"replay:coordination: two identities use one place",
"Post-hoc on one incident: these four alarms were picked as the main early warning after seeing that they fired with more harm still to come than the shared-control signs on the Swarm Traces release. Their thresholds were not tuned, but the choice of alarms (and of the 6 h volume history over the 12 h one) was made with that answer in view, so their figures on that release are not a test.",
"Not an early warning. These signs say which identities share a place, a token, a program or a message, which is what an investigator needs after an alarm. On the real release they fired later than every simple alarm, and on simulated swarms the shared-place sign fires after the first harm.",
